# Every variable here is OPTIONAL. RepoCanary's detector is pure static
# analysis: it needs no keys at all, and the site works with this file empty.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI second opinion: not configured here
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The site deliberately reads NO AI provider key. The optional second opinion
# runs on the visitor's own key, supplied in the form, used for that single
# request and never stored. A key set here would be spent by strangers, and
# rationing it would mean identifying visitors, which is the one thing a tool
# for people who are being targeted must not do.
#
# The CLI is where keys belong, because there the key and the bill are the
# same person's. `npx repocanary <url> --ai` reads GEMINI_API_KEY,
# GROQ_API_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY or ANTHROPIC_API_KEY from your environment, in
# that order, with GEMINI_MODEL, GROQ_MODEL, OPENAI_MODEL and ANTHROPIC_MODEL
# to override the model. Gemini and Groq issue free keys; the other two bill
# per scan. See the README.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional token (classic or fine-grained, public repo read only). Raises the
# GitHub API rate limit from 60 to 5,000 requests per hour. Without it a busy
# site will hit the limit, and scans then fail honestly rather than returning
# a false green.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Site
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Canonical site URL, used for the canonical link, Open Graph and Twitter
# image URLs, robots.txt, and sitemap. Set this only when the site serves a
# domain other than the canonical one in web/lib/siteurl.ts. Unset, a
# production build uses that canonical domain and a development server uses
# localhost:3000. No hosting platform is consulted.
#
# Whatever host this names must serve the current build: social previews load
# the image from it, so a stale deployment there shows a stale preview.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-domain.com
